<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamasee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yamasee were a Native American people of the coastal region of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>. Allied with the English of Carolina, they raided Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> and its Native peoples for captives in the late 17th and early 18th centuries. Abuses by English traders led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamasee-war">Yamasee War</a> of 1715–1717, after which most survivors moved to Spanish Florida.</p></div>
